course: dictionary
lesson: 9755
title: Who is in charge?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A supervisor is a person whose job is to watch over other people and their work, and make sure things are done right and safely. Look for the clue words: watch, right and safely all show that a supervisor is in charge of keeping things in order.
explain: At school, a lunchtime supervisor is an adult who watches children at lunch, in the playground or during an exam. «If you spill a drink, you tell a lunch supervisor and help clean it up, because wet floors make people slip.» The supervisor is the grown-up you tell, so they can stop someone getting hurt.
explain: Outside school, a supervisor is often the boss of a small team in a shop, factory or office. Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Tell the person in charge about the spill» still makes sense, so you have understood supervisor.
fact: A supervisor is a person whose job is to watch over other people and their work.
fact: A supervisor makes sure things are done right and safely.
fact: At school, a lunchtime supervisor is an adult who watches children at lunch, in the playground or during an exam.
fact: «Lunchtime supervisor», «talk to your supervisor» and «under supervision» are useful phrases to know.
fact: «Under supervision» means being watched over by a responsible adult.
exercise: Who do you tell if you spill a drink at lunch? | Your best friend, who will fix it | Nobody, just wipe it with your sleeve | *A lunch supervisor | The gate at the end of the playground
exercise: What is a supervisor's job? | Playing games with children in the playground | Selling things in a shop | Cooking the lunch for the whole school | *Watching over people and their work, and making sure things are done right and safely
exercise: In «tell a supervisor about spills so nobody slips», why do you tell the supervisor? | To be first in the lunch queue | *To keep people from slipping and getting hurt | To get a sticker for being helpful | To make the floor wetter
test: What does «under supervision» mean? | Being underneath the table | Being in a great hurry | Being very quiet and still | *Being watched over by a responsible adult
test: Ella's dad is a supervisor in a factory. What does his job mean? | He makes the machines in the factory | He cleans the factory floor every night | *He is in charge of a small team and makes sure their work is done right and safely | He sells the factory's products in a shop
exam: Sam says a supervisor is a type of playground tag. Why is Sam wrong? | *A supervisor is a person whose job is to watch over other people and their work | A supervisor is always a child | A supervisor is a dish served at lunch | Tag is played with a ball, not with people
